# CARD-3 · A card that failed, handed again, then withdrawn (real Claude
# Code: the leader does each with its own tools when asked).
start --budget 3
see any key: close
key Escape
key /
type Hire one worker on the cheap tier and assign it a card titled Import books, with this task: say done with outcome failed at once, writing nothing.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
allow 600 failed
key /
type Assign card #1 again, to a new worker on the cheap tier, with the same task.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
# A second hire waits for the plan's yes.
# The leader hands it again: to the same worker, or a new one after a
# plan's yes; either way the journal says the try.
key J
key J
allow 600 try 2 || planned 1 card
key Escape
key g d
key a
key J
key J
allow 600 try 2
key Escape
# A card that waits on it (`after`), posted now so it changes nothing of
# the tries above.
key /
type Post a card titled Shelve books with the same task, to be taken only after card 1 (after: [1]). Do nothing else.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
key J
key J
allow 300 posted #2
key Escape
key /
type Withdraw card #1, saying it is not needed.
key Enter
key Escape Escape
# imece's words, never the leader's: the card after it says what became
# of the one it waits on.
allow 600 waits on #1 which was
# On the board it stands done, marked – and its try.
type :board
key Enter
see · try 2
# The card after it never begins: it says what it waited on.
see ✕ #1 withdrawn
key Escape
